{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/297728-character-idea-help","id":297728,"title":"Character idea help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-30T19:39:03-07:00","id":297728,"title":"Character idea help","content":"My group may end up trying Scion sometime soon, so I've been coming up with some character concepts in anticipation of this. The one I've settled on is a Native American(don't know tribe yet) bar owner. He's inspired by <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I2J0i5qBeSs\" target=\"_blank\">Chayton Littlestone</a> from the show &quot;Banshee&quot;, somewhat. He's going to be big, scary big, and have Epic Strength and Stamina. I still haven't figured out what god is going to be his parent, but I'm guessing it will end up being a war god due to his warrior nature. But that's not what I'm looking for help on. What I'm looking for help on is another aspect of him; intimidation and fear.<br /> <br /> I figure he'll end up being a physically impressive man, the kind other people naturally fear. I'm not sure what Epic Attribute would govern what I'm going for. I want him to be the kind of person that draws attention, fear, and envy. When he walks into a room, people stop and stare. When he looks at someone, they generally shrink down to avoid his gaze or just pee their pants. When he speaks, people shut up and listen because they can't really think to do otherwise. People are drawn to him because he exudes sheer power, and they feel safer when they're on the same side as him. I just can't figure out what attribute would apply here. I was originally thinking Appearance, but I don't really see him as either good looking or ugly. I was thinking Manipulation might fit with the intimidation aspect, but I see his as brutally honest and straight forward. Charisma might work, but I want him to be able to affect others with just a glance.<br /> <br /> It's possible I'm looking at a combination of different attributes, and not just a single one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T00:51:37-07:00","id":297918,"title":"","content":"Epic Appearance does, in fact, have Knacks that will help you. Do Not Want, Dreadful Mein, Game Face, Serpent's Gaze, Inescapable Vision... in fact, most of them are pretty handy for that kind of character. You can spin Epic Appearance a number of ways. Negative Appearance doesn't have to be hideously malformed. It can be a creeping terror, or something subtly <i>wrong</i> about the character. I've played a PC with Epic Negative whose teeth were too white, too sharp, and sometimes his beard was streaked with dried blood. Hunger lurked in his eyes, and the size of him always seemed to bring to mind how easily he could break bones or tear off limbs. He was heavy on Epic Appearance (he could also turn on the animal magnetism if he needed to, thanks to Visage Great and Terrible) and Epic Charisma, in addition to his physical stats.<br /> <br /> Charisma is also handy, but you're right, affecting people just by <i>being around</i> is pretty much what Appearance is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T11:27:45-07:00","id":298315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/297728-character-idea-help?p=297918#post297918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Epic Appearance does, in fact, have Knacks that will help you. Do Not Want, Dreadful Mein, Game Face, Serpent's Gaze, Inescapable Vision... in fact, most of them are pretty handy for that kind of character. You can spin Epic Appearance a number of ways. Negative Appearance doesn't have to be hideously malformed. It can be a creeping terror, or something subtly <i>wrong</i> about the character. I've played a PC with Epic Negative whose teeth were too white, too sharp, and sometimes his beard was streaked with dried blood. Hunger lurked in his eyes, and the size of him always seemed to bring to mind how easily he could break bones or tear off limbs. He was heavy on Epic Appearance (he could also turn on the animal magnetism if he needed to, thanks to Visage Great and Terrible) and Epic Charisma, in addition to his physical stats.<br /> <br /> Charisma is also handy, but you're right, affecting people just by <i>being around</i> is pretty much what Appearance is for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I got hung up on the beautiful/ugly aspect of Appearance and that was why I wasn't sure at first. I'm going to go for Appearance now and just describe him as striking and impressive, not necessarily pretty or horrific. Thanks for the help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3716-mrtwist","name":"Mrtwist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T18:15:27-07:00","id":299519,"title":"","content":"My suggestion? Make him a child of Hades, but have Ares adopt him. He inherits the death god's grim and passionless demeanor, but Ares keeps wanting him to go on killing sprees. Really, what's scarier than someone who slaughters enemies by the thousands and seems complete disinterested in it while he does so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-02-2014, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}